WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.790
If you want to hear about how Mordeo, the
Crypt monster series we talked about last

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.540
week on Things You Missed, could tie into
Shelley, the Crypt monster series I’m gonna

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.490
talk about today, then stick around to the
end of this video.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:14.020
Today’s video was made possible by our sponsor
Crypt TV.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.880
The first episode of Season 2 of Shelley has
just come out and as with all of Crypt’s

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.400
2019 productions it’s all part of a greater
universe.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.310
There are little clues hidden throughout,
about how this all fits in with the grand

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:30.289
story that each of these series make up.

00:00:30.289 --> 00:00:34.020
But before we get into my theory about how
Shelley Season 2 fits into this universe,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.950
let’s take a quick look back at Season 1.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.720
Season 1 takes place 20 years after the 1998
graduation at Avon Manor High School, where

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:45.720
an introverted floor hockey athlete hangs
by the neck at the graduation ceremony.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.960
The story follows Nicks, Lauren and Heidi,
three bullies who picked on Shelley and other

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.480
girls back in the day.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.350
At the reunion, Heidi fires an insult at a
girl names Celine, by bringing up her old

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.890
nickname Blobby.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:01.290
Lauren excuses herself to go to the bathroom,
where she has a flashback of them bullying

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.870
Shelley, calling her Silent Shelley, and tightening
her tie around her neck.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.520
“Can you talk now?

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.520
Huh?”

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.119
Uhh, no probably not.

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:13.200
You’re kind of blocking her wind-pipe thing.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.720
Lauren is attacked by a monster resembling
Shelley.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.259
When Nicks and Heidi go looking for her, after
discovering an old photo of when Shelley was

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:23.780
just a Lv 1 crook, they find Lauren’s jaw
has been removed, possibly intended as a literal

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.840
silencing in response to their “Silent Shelley”
taunts.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.060
A tie is also tightened around her neck.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.920
They see this as a sign that someone knows
their secret, but that secret is not yet revealed.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.100
In the next scene, Heidi and Nicks run into
the locker room.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.770
Here’s a little free tip for you.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:41.689
If the ghost of student athlete is haunting
you, don’t go in the locker room, literally

00:01:41.689 --> 00:01:43.130
go anywhere else.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:46.850
Nicks gets picked off with a mean slapshot,
leaving just Heidi remaining.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:49.670
Throughout the school there are posters advertising
a production of MacBeth.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.490
This is a fitting reference, because MacBeth
is a Shakespeare character who becomes riddled

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.310
with guilt after committing a murder.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:58.509
We soon find that this is the case with the
bullies as well.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:02.689
That little neck tie incident actually killed
Shelley or at least incapacitated her, so

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:07.240
the girls make it look like a suicide, and
almost get away with it if not for Celine,

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.590
aka Blobby, catching them in the act.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:13.820
The pursuer reveals herself to be none other
than Celine and Heidi is chased into what

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.140
appears to be that MacBeth production.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:20.500
She almost gets away, but there’s a second
killer, the real Shelley, who finally gets

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.500
her revenge.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.640
Hand in hand, we see that Celine and Shelley
have matching bracelets and there’s a little

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.510
post-credits scene hinting that in Season
2, Shelley is going to target the school’s

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.510
staff.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:32.360
That’s where this theory takes off, with
this symbol in the school administration’s

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.360
office.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.870
It appears to be a ripped out page of the
book, The Crypt Tome, which is a manual for

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:40.050
men to turn themselves into monsters that
appears in several Crypt series'.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:44.031
This symbol in particular is the emblem seen
on the Door in the Woods, a Crypt Monster

00:02:44.031 --> 00:02:47.840
Universe short film about a colony sworn to
protect the world from a monster known as

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.840
The Brute.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.930
The Brute is basically a level 50 boss.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:54.410
The symbol is seen on the door and on the
clothing of everyone in the colony.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:58.270
My theory is that the schools in Shelley are
built on the ground upon which this colony

00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.270
once resided.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:01.370
That’s right, I said schools, plural.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:05.901
It seems that Shelley’s school, Avon Manor,
is an all-girls school located next to the

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:06.901
all-boys school.

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:10.460
The headmaster of Avon Manor even says that
there are multiple schools when she talks

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.060
on the phone with Hargate, who is presumably
in charge of the boys’ school.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.680
“Our schools are being disgraced.”

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.080
On top of that, in this shot of Hargate’s
office, there is a picture of the boys’

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.960
school’s crest, which is different than
the Avon Manor crest.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:27.910
The symbol of Avon Manor is a fox, but this
school seems to have a stag -- which interestingly

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:30.350
enough, is the animal head of Mordeo.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:34.340
This is a pretty small detail, and it remains
to be seen if there will really be any crossover,

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:36.060
but it’s definitely something to keep an
eye on.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.660
But there’s definitely a connection with
The Door In Woods, and I believe it has something

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.430
to do with the bracelet that Shelly recovers
from Celine, which is seen to been originally

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:47.130
given to her by this guy, who I would assume
is Shelley’s boyfriend from the boy’s

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.130
school.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:51.190
The bracelet is seen at the end of the episode
giving life to this buried person.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:54.740
Maybe this is the reason that Brute and Shelley
are seemingly invincible.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:59.260
This revival ritual, likely taken out of the
Crypt Tome, could bring its subject back to

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:02.319
life and give them new monstrous powers.

00:04:02.319 --> 00:04:05.870
Shelley also has similar themes to The Door
In The Woods, with adults trying to keep this

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:09.750
ancient power hidden away from the kids, and
the rest of the world in both stories.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.560
“Having people snooping around could ruin
us.”

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.780
So it would appear that after all this time,
the powers in charge of the colony are still

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.190
trying to supress the evil that lies within.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.090
Let me know what you think of this theory
in the comments and any other thoughts you

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:29.320
have on Shelley, The Door In The Woods, Mordeo,
and anything else that could be connected

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.320
to this storyline.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.130
Of course you’ll want to stay tuned to this
entire season of Shelley.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:37.780
Remember to subscribe to Crypt TV for new
Crypt Monster Universe videos every Friday,

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:41.940
ring the deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next one.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:43.860
Assuming we both survive.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.410
Or get brought back.

